Dear OEIS editors,

Please consider the attached b084945.txt as a b-file for A084945
(Decimal expansion of the Golomb-Dickman constant), replacing the
current synthesized b-file for n = 0..101.

Link text:

Konstantin Pozdnyakov, <a href="b084945.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n=0..39999</a>

Suggested comment:

Terms 0..39999 computed using certified interval arithmetic (Arb).

The 40,000 digits are backed by a certificate, not by a floating-point
computation. The certificate gives integers Lambda_- < Lambda_+ and a
scale S = 133074 with

    floor(10^40000 * Lambda_- / 2^S)
  = floor(10^40000 * Lambda_+ / 2^S),

so the interval cannot cross a decimal boundary and the 40,000-digit
truncation is proved. Its width is about 10^-40042.26.

Certificate, verifier and code:
https://github.com/fix27/golomb-dickman-constant/tree/main/40000

SHA-256 of b084945.txt:
c73af643198da299d2e624e3c2f69d05439efcddbbefa7cec176ac63f993bed3

The file is plain ASCII with LF line endings, 40,000 terms, indices
0..39999, one trailing blank line, 308,891 bytes, 40,001 lines.

Verification needs only Python 3.11+ and the standard library:

    python verify_40000.py
    OK: 40000 digits certified

The first 102 digits agree with the published A084945 data, and every
term of the b-file is checked against the certificate.

If 40,000 terms is considered too long, the same file can be truncated
to 10,000 or 20,000 terms on request; the prefix is unchanged.

